from pathlib import Path
r=Path.cwd();p=r/'tools/build-guides.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');position=s.index('user_order = [')
chapters='''USER.append(('Inspect column types defaults and constraints', [
'Choose Database schema in the upper-right page selector after opening the intended project or cache. Select column in the kind selector and declared column in the evidence-state selector. Select a row to read Declared type, Nullability declaration and Default declaration at the top of the labeled memo. Columns are the named fields declared within a table. A data type describes the declared representation of a field; a default is a captured expression used when an applicable database operation omits a value; a constraint states a rule. DPH captures those declarations without executing or validating them against a server.',
'Explicit NULL and explicit NOT NULL identify clauses actually present in that column entry. Not declared means absent from that entry, not an inferred effective default or permission to store nulls. Primary keys, domains, inherited schema and later migrations can affect effective rules; their implications are not synthesized into explicit declarations. DEFAULT NULL is a default expression and does not become an explicit nullability clause. Numeric, symbolic, simple function and parenthesized defaults retain captured text. String literal contents are replaced by a visible literal omitted marker. Nothing is evaluated.',
'Inline constraints show captured NOT NULL, NULL, PRIMARY KEY, UNIQUE, REFERENCES and CHECK text, including supported named clauses. Choose constraint and captured constraint to read table-level entries separately. A CHECK expression can contain commas without splitting the table incorrectly. Constraint text does not establish key membership, referenced-column relationships, valid expression semantics or deployed enforcement. Those are separate investigations. Every column retains the original source line, SHA256, generation and exact parent table declaration identity, so duplicate table definitions cannot silently merge their columns.',
'Filter by table or column name, source file, declared type such as DECIMAL, explicit nullability or inline constraint text. Combine this with kind and state filters. First page and Next page show 250 matches; scroll commands sideways in a narrow window. Unsupported column clauses, missing types/default expressions and conflicting explicit nullability become gaps with the full sanitized entry and an explanation. Later supported entries remain inspectable. Open source uses the existing attached-source hash and generation guards. Read docs/guides/Database_Columns_Run_and_Test.txt for complete directions and controlled practice.'
]))
ENGINEERING.append(('Extract captured column declarations and constraint text', [
'TDPHDatabaseSchema.Inspect extends the existing resource-token projection. It splits CREATE TABLE body entries only at outer commas, retaining type precision, CHECK and default-function commas. Supported entries emit column rows with declared_type, nullability, default, constraints, table and declaration_id. Explicit table-level constraint entries emit captured constraint text rows. These facts describe captured syntax, not a validated live schema. PostgreSQL CREATE TABLE documentation supplies the reference structure; this bounded reader is not a full dialect grammar.',
'Type text accepts an identifier or qualified type, supported multiword suffixes, parenthesized parameters, time-zone qualifiers and array or unsigned suffixes. Clause extraction distinguishes DEFAULT NULL from explicit NULL, accepts bounded simple or parenthesized defaults, and captures supported named and inline constraints. String contents remain omitted. Token-aware formatting preserves quoted identifier spelling while presenting readable numeric and type evidence. Unsupported clauses, absent types, incomplete defaults, repeated defaults, conflicting NULL/NOT NULL and trailing empty entries remain gaps. A supported later entry does not inherit the preceding gap.',
'Each column and table-level constraint keeps a unique parent declaration ID plus original file, source SHA256, generation and entry-start line. Duplicate table declarations retain independent column facts instead of selecting an effective migration. Whole-resource byte extents remain explicitly labeled. Key relationships, domain/inheritance rules, expression evaluation, dialect validity and deployed enforcement are unverified. No analyzer schema migration, target driver connection or runtime control construction is introduced.',
'DPH.UI.Main.fmx adds column/constraint kinds and declared column/captured constraint states to existing Object Inspector editable selectors. Existing filter logic also searches declared type, explicit nullability and inline constraint text. Details lead with column type/nullability/default before long provenance explanations, improving compact-window use. Existing 250-row pages, capture replacement, labeled scrolling memo and guarded source navigation remain in use.',
'Run tools/build-database-columns.cmd elevated for 121 checks using actual controlled project/resource analysis, SQLite persisted reopening, native FMX filtering/details/paging and normal/compact PaintTo renders. Checks cover type precision, multiword and qualified/quoted types, defaults, NULL separation, named/inline/table constraint text, nested commas, unsupported entries, duplicate declaration ownership, literal canaries and unchanged source/catalog/workspace. Existing schema and engine suites add 123 regression checks. Actual application build and FMX baseline pass. Fixed ignored bin/database-columns-validation contains controlled practice data. No SQL or target application is executed.'
]))
for chapters in (USER, ENGINEERING):
 for index, (heading, paragraphs) in enumerate(chapters):
  chapters[index]=(heading,[p.replace('333 requirement records remain incomplete','332 requirement records remain incomplete') for p in paragraphs])

'''
